**Read:** [Ironmaking and Steelmaking — Gour Gopal Roy, NPTEL](../sources/Ironmaking-and-Steelmaking-NPTEL.lingua#r_0XJNFP35VJ24ZR6AZJ78EY03G0), the complete first five weeks and the full direct/smelting-reduction sequence; [Iron and Steel Production — European Commission BREF](../sources/Iron-and-Steel-Production-BREF.lingua#r_1R9HC6SENF991ZZQA5WKH2C8HD), whole raw-material, agglomeration, and ironmaking chapters; [Materials, energy, and heat balances in metallurgical processes — Satish Ch. Koria](../sources/Metallurgical-Material-and-Heat-Balances-NPTEL.lingua#r_38NWQRDJH3RVM3NNGB71RR1X43), all ironmaking material/heat and RIST exercises.

An iron-bearing feed is characterized by phase chemistry, iron/impurity content, gangue, size/form, porosity, mechanical/thermal/reduction behavior, and variability. The target is a usable intermediate for the selected steel or casting route, with its actual carbon, impurity, physical, and thermal requirements.

Reuse sampling, beneficiation, agglomeration, reduction, slag, and balance principles instead of treating ironmaking as an unrelated collection of equipment. Burden permeability, strength/reactivity, reducing-gas access, heat, softening/melting, and slag quantities interact. A feed with a favorable bulk iron grade may have a consequential physical or impurity limitation.

Compare blast-furnace, direct-reduction, smelting-reduction, and secondary-metal routes on matched material/output boundaries. Include the actual reductant, gas/electricity, agglomeration, equipment, water, product handling, and supporting work. A route's claimed benefit depends on those conditions and on the later steelmaking quality account.

**Work:** reconstruct two complete iron-feed/route cases from primary teaching and technical material. Independently calculate iron and gangue/impurity flows and a defensible energy basis. Compare alternative feed qualities and test a changed utility or availability condition. Explain which observations support the preferred route and what remains unproven about scale, product quality, or downstream compatibility.

**Continue:** [Reconstruct a blast furnace through coupled reduction, heat, flow, and material behavior](Blast-furnace-reduction-heat-gas-flow-and-burden.lingua#r_4KZ0TXMQ2WAT83FCPAEVVTMEV6).

**Return:** [Metals and metallurgical production — feed, refining, structure, useful products, and recovery](../Metals-and-metallurgical-production.lingua#r_59BDAQXT81552YF5F8TH4KQQH1).
